# Token & maintenance optimization

Future agents must leave the codebase *more* optimized than they found it when the change is in scope. Do not only fix the asked bug/feature and ignore obvious locality debt in touched files.

## Before writing code

1. Read `AGENTS.md` feature entry points and Shared patterns.
2. Prefer existing helpers over new copies: `@/utils/id`, `@/utils/parse`, `@/utils/pick-image` (`pickCameraImage` / `pickLibraryImage` / `pickLibraryImages`), `@/utils/image-persist`, `@/utils/confirm-destructive`, `@/services/http/api-url` + `api-client`, `@/services/ai/vision-transport`, `LoadingBlock`, `DateField`, `appPrompt`.
3. Open the smallest entry file first; do not load sibling giants unless needed.

## When editing large screens

- If a touched screen/module is **>700 lines** and you add non-trivial UI, extract a focused panel/helper into a colocated file instead of growing the monolith.
- Keep orchestration (state, store calls, navigation) in the screen; move presentational sections + their styles out.
- Update the `AGENTS.md` feature entry table when you add a new entry module.

## Never reintroduce

- Raw `Alert` / `ActionSheetIOS` for app UI
- Ad-hoc UUID/`Date.now()` ID generators when `@/utils/id` fits
- Duplicate camera/library permission + picker flows
- Duplicate Cancel+destructive `appPrompt.alert` when `confirmDestructiveAction` fits
- Parallel API URL/fetch helpers when `resolveExpoApiUrl` / `apiRequest` fit
- Parallel OpenAI/Ollama vision transport when `vision-transport` fits
- Persisting image-picker cache URIs (always re-encode via image helpers)

## After substantive edits

- Run `npm run typecheck` and relevant `npm test` for touched domains.
- If you discovered a reusable pattern used in 3+ places while fixing something else, extract it in the same change when safe.
